---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "8595 Moraine Drive | A Pricing Proposal from Mark Gores";
const description = "A pricing proposal prepared by Mark Gores for Ryan and Kerrie Schwertman at 8595 Moraine Drive, Shakopee.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} noindex={true}>

<nav class="proposal-nav">
  <a href="/" class="name">Mark Gores</a>
  <div class="nav-meta">Prepared for Ryan &amp; Kerrie Schwertman · April 2026</div>
</nav>

<main class="proposal">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="prop-hero">
    <div class="prop-hero-content">
      <div class="prop-label">A Pricing Proposal</div>
      <h1>For Ryan &amp; Kerrie<br><em>8595 Moraine Drive, Shakopee</em></h1>
      <p class="prop-hero-text">
        Thanks again for having me over. Rather than send a PDF your way, I built you a page. What I think you should list it at, how I got to that number, the comps I'm leaning on, how I'd market the house, and a net sheet showing what you'd walk away with.
      </p>
      <div class="prop-signature">Mark</div>
    </div>
    <div class="prop-hero-image">
      <img src="/images/8595-moraine-front.jpg" alt="8595 Moraine Drive, Shakopee" />
      <div class="photo-caption">Prior listing photo. You've since painted the front of the house.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE RECOMMENDATION -->
  <section class="recommendation">
    <div class="section-label-alt">The Number</div>
    <h2>List at <em>$565,000</em></h2>
    <p class="rec-sub">
      Expected sale price: <strong>$560,000 to $570,000</strong><br>
      Expected days on market: <strong>Under 14</strong>
    </p>

    <div class="rec-why">
      <p>
        Here's how I got there. I pulled six comps that match your house pretty closely. Then I looked at three recent sales on Moraine itself. Then I looked at 8490 Moraine, which is currently under contract at $639,990. The data lines up cleanly, your updates earn you a real premium, and this number gives us room to negotiate without leaving money on the table.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="rec-range">
      <div class="range-card">
        <div class="range-label">Safe</div>
        <div class="range-price">$549,000</div>
        <div class="range-note">The most conservative of the three. Prioritizes certainty over maximizing the number.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="range-card recommended">
        <div class="range-label">Recommended</div>
        <div class="range-price">$565,000</div>
        <div class="range-note">Where the comps, the street, and your updates all point when I put them together.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="range-card">
        <div class="range-label">Stretch</div>
        <div class="range-price">$579,000</div>
        <div class="range-note">Tests the Glacier Estates ceiling. Takes patience and a great photo package.</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rec-note">
      <div class="rec-note-label">A quick note on the round number</div>
      <p>
        Real estate pricing wisdom used to say "end in 9" (list at $564,900 instead of $565,000). The data I've looked at just doesn't back that up anymore, especially at this price point. Round numbers signal confidence, they show up in more Zillow and Realtor searches (buyers filter in $25k and $50k chunks), and you get to keep the extra hundred bucks. I'd rather that money end up in your pocket than lost in a pricing superstition.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SUBJECT SPECS -->
  <section class="specs">
    <div class="section-label-alt">The Home</div>
    <h2>What makes your house, your house.</h2>
    <div class="specs-grid">
      <div class="spec"><div class="spec-v">2006</div><div class="spec-l">Year Built</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="spec-v">2,669</div><div class="spec-l">Finished Sq Ft</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="spec-v">1,269</div><div class="spec-l">Foundation</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="spec-v">4 / 3</div><div class="spec-l">Bed / Bath</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="spec-v">3-car</div><div class="spec-l">Garage</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="spec-v">0.30 ac</div><div class="spec-l">Lot Size</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="spec-v">Walkout</div><div class="spec-l">Basement (unfinished)</div></div>
      <div class="spec"><div class="spec-v">Glacier Estates</div><div class="spec-l">Subdivision</div></div>
    </div>
    <p class="specs-narrative">
      You've done real work on the main floor. New flooring throughout, cabinetry updated to a crisp white, the very cool looking blue center island, and beautiful new countertops. In this price range, buyers are choosing between "move-in ready" and "needs $20k in cosmetics." Your updates put you solidly in the first bucket, and the comps below show what that's worth. And the unfinished walkout is a plus, not a downside. Natural light, a real door to the yard, and a buyer can finish it on their own timeline if they want more square footage.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- COMPARABLE SALES -->
  <section class="comps">
    <div class="section-label-alt">The Comps</div>
    <h2>Six recent sales, matched on size, age, and basement status.</h2>
    <p class="comps-intro">
      Every one of these closed in the last twelve months in Shakopee. All 4 bed, 3 bath, similar square footage, and all with unfinished basements. That last part matters. If I let a comp with a finished lower level sneak in, it throws the whole thing off, so I kept it apples to apples.
    </p>

    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="comp-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Address</th>
            <th class="r">Sold</th>
            <th class="r">Date</th>
            <th class="r">SqFt</th>
            <th class="r">Lot</th>
            <th class="r">Yr</th>
            <th class="r">$/SF</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>1791 Rye Court<br><span class="sub">Riverside Fields</span></td>
            <td class="r">$450,000</td>
            <td class="r">2/26/26</td>
            <td class="r">2,198</td>
            <td class="r">0.14</td>
            <td class="r">2008</td>
            <td class="r">$205</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>1895 Omega Drive<br><span class="sub">Wyndam Ponds</span></td>
            <td class="r">$490,000</td>
            <td class="r">12/31/25</td>
            <td class="r">2,420</td>
            <td class="r">0.29</td>
            <td class="r">2004</td>
            <td class="r">$202</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>2124 Winterberry Lane<br><span class="sub">Park Meadows</span></td>
            <td class="r">$507,500</td>
            <td class="r">7/03/25</td>
            <td class="r">2,427</td>
            <td class="r">0.25</td>
            <td class="r">2005</td>
            <td class="r">$209</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>1715 Lusitano Street<br><span class="sub">Countryside</span></td>
            <td class="r">$524,900</td>
            <td class="r">7/01/25</td>
            <td class="r">2,460</td>
            <td class="r">0.26</td>
            <td class="r">2006</td>
            <td class="r">$213</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>571 Jutland Avenue<br><span class="sub">Countryside</span></td>
            <td class="r">$550,000</td>
            <td class="r">4/30/25</td>
            <td class="r">2,813</td>
            <td class="r">0.27</td>
            <td class="r">2008</td>
            <td class="r">$196</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>9109 Edgewood Circle<br><span class="sub">Whispering Oaks</span></td>
            <td class="r">$580,000</td>
            <td class="r">10/14/25</td>
            <td class="r">2,420</td>
            <td class="r">0.44</td>
            <td class="r">2006</td>
            <td class="r">$240</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="summary">
            <td><strong>Median / Average</strong></td>
            <td class="r"><strong>$516k / $517k</strong></td>
            <td class="r">avg</td>
            <td class="r">2,443</td>
            <td class="r">0.28</td>
            <td class="r">2006</td>
            <td class="r"><strong>$211</strong></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="callout">
      <div class="callout-label">Adjusted to your home</div>
      <p>
        When I size-adjust each of these to your 2,669 finished sq ft and factor in lot and garage differences, the adjusted average lands right around <strong>$530,000</strong>. Think of that as the floor. None of these six sold comps are on Moraine Drive, and none of them are walkouts like yours, so your number should land higher.
      </p>
    </div>

    <a class="portal-link" href="https://portal.onehome.com/en-US/share/1002656D60092" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
      <span class="portal-arrow">→</span>
      <span>
        <span class="portal-title">Click through all seven properties</span>
        <span class="portal-sub">Photos, room details, full listings for all six comps plus 8490 Moraine. I set up a portal so you can scroll them yourself.</span>
      </span>
    </a>
  </section>

  <!-- GLACIER ESTATES PROOF -->
  <section class="street-proof">
    <div class="street-inner">
      <div class="section-label-alt light">The Street Premium</div>
      <h2>Moraine Drive doesn't sell like a typical Shakopee subdivision.</h2>
      <p>
        Here's the part most agents miss. Similar homes on similar streets sell at one price. Similar homes in <em>Glacier Estates</em> sell at another. Worth paying attention to when we set your list price.
      </p>

      <div class="street-grid">
        <div class="street-card">
          <div class="street-addr">8429 Moraine</div>
          <div class="street-sold">$610,000</div>
          <div class="street-meta">Sold 6/17/25 · 11 DOM<br>3,002 sf · finished LL · 2007</div>
        </div>
        <div class="street-card">
          <div class="street-addr">8530 Moraine</div>
          <div class="street-sold">$564,900</div>
          <div class="street-meta">Sold 5/08/24 · 2 DOM<br>2,778 sf · unfinished · 2012</div>
        </div>
        <div class="street-card">
          <div class="street-addr">8560 Moraine</div>
          <div class="street-sold">$554,000</div>
          <div class="street-meta">Sold 2/28/24 · 9 DOM<br>2,966 sf · unfinished · 2012</div>
        </div>
        <div class="street-card active">
          <div class="street-addr">8490 Moraine</div>
          <div class="street-sold">$639,990<span class="list-tag">LIST</span></div>
          <div class="street-meta">Active · Currently under contract<br>4,344 sf · finished · 2012</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="street-takeaway">
        Your neighbors sell fast and sell well. When I time-adjust 8530 and 8560 to today's market, they roll forward to roughly <strong>$595k to $605k</strong> at their spec. Your house is smaller and your lower level isn't finished, so we can't quite chase those numbers. But you absolutely earn a premium over comps on other streets. That's how I landed at $565,000.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE ACTIVE LISTINGS -->
  <section class="actives">
    <div class="section-label-alt">The Active Listings</div>
    <h2>What else is on the market right now.</h2>
    <p class="actives-intro">
      Three other resale homes are currently listed in Shakopee between $525K and $575K. I looked at each one:
    </p>
    <ul class="actives-list">
      <li><strong>$525,000</strong> &nbsp;·&nbsp; 2001 build with a walkout and a finished lower level, but only a 2-car garage on a 0.17 acre lot, few updates, and marketing photos that don't do it any favors. <span class="dom-tag">26 days on market</span></li>
      <li><strong>$559,999</strong> &nbsp;·&nbsp; 3-bedroom with 2,500 total sq ft, basement only partially finished. <span class="dom-tag">109 days on market</span></li>
      <li><strong>$569,500</strong> &nbsp;·&nbsp; 3-level split with 2,496 total finished sq ft. <span class="dom-tag">Just hit the market yesterday</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="actives-takeaway">
      They're different homes chasing different buyers. There are also about 20 new-construction listings active in the area, but new construction tends to pull a different buyer entirely.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- MARKETING PLAN -->
  <section class="marketing">
    <div class="section-label-alt">The Marketing Plan</div>
    <h2>What you get, for one flat fee.</h2>
    <p class="marketing-intro">
      No upsells. No "premium package" tiers. No marketing fund add-on. Everything below is included for every client, no exceptions.
    </p>

    <div class="marketing-grid">
      <div class="marketing-card">
        <h3>Pre-Listing</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Professional staging consultation</li>
          <li>Pricing strategy &amp; list price review</li>
          <li>Pre-inspection guidance if needed</li>
          <li>Photo-ready punch list walkthrough</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="marketing-card">
        <h3>Photography &amp; Media</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Professional interior &amp; exterior photography</li>
          <li>Aerial / drone photography</li>
          <li>Listing description written by me, not an AI</li>
          <li><strong>Written caption on every MLS photo</strong> (most agents skip this; captions help tell more of the story behind each room)</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="marketing-card">
        <h3>Advertising &amp; Exposure</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Full NorthstarMLS listing &amp; syndication</li>
          <li>Targeted online advertising</li>
          <li>Social media campaign</li>
          <li>Print advertising</li>
          <li>Radio advertising</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="marketing-card">
        <h3>Communication</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Weekly written updates</strong> with showing activity, buyer feedback, and listing analytics</li>
          <li>Direct access to me by phone or text, not a team or an assistant</li>
          <li>Honest feedback when something needs to change (price, staging, photos)</li>
          <li>Regular check-ins through closing, not just until the contract is signed</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="marketing-card">
        <h3>Offers &amp; Negotiation</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>Showing coordination &amp; feedback tracking</li>
          <li>Offer review with a written breakdown of terms, not just price</li>
          <li>Negotiation strategy based on 22 years of reading buyers' agents</li>
          <li>Contract-to-close management, inspections, appraisal, and title</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="marketing-card">
        <h3>Local Expertise</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>22 years working the south metro, Shakopee and Prior Lake specifically</li>
          <li>First-hand familiarity with every comp I'm leaning on</li>
          <li>Relationships with local lenders, inspectors, stagers, and title</li>
          <li>Live on-the-ground market data I pull myself every 15 minutes</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FEE STRUCTURE -->
  <section class="fees">
    <div class="section-label-alt">The Fees</div>
    <h2>2.5%. Reduced for 2026.</h2>

    <p class="fees-intro">
      I'm quietly building software that does in minutes what used to take me hours. Pulling live market data, comparing neighborhood comps, building pricing models, tracking every listing across the south metro. A Shakopee version of the site is coming soon (I already have the data pulling in). <a href="https://priorlake.realestate" target="_blank" rel="noopener">PriorLake.RealEstate</a> is the first public version if you want to see the kind of thing I'm building.
    </p>
    <p class="fees-intro">
      Those tools genuinely lower my cost to serve you. I'd rather pass that savings straight to my sellers than keep the difference. So my listing fee in 2026 is <strong>2.5%</strong>, about half a point less than the typical full-service agent in this market. Same service, better data, lower cost.
    </p>

    <div class="fees-breakdown">
      <div class="fee-row">
        <div class="fee-label">
          <div class="fee-title">My listing fee</div>
          <div class="fee-sub">Everything on the marketing plan above is included.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="fee-amount"><strong>2.5%</strong></div>
      </div>
      <div class="fee-row">
        <div class="fee-label">
          <div class="fee-title">Buyer's agent compensation</div>
          <div class="fee-sub">Since the 2024 NAR settlement, this is a separate negotiation. Locally it's still usually around 2.7%, and sometimes we can get it down to 2.5%. I'd plan on 2.7% for now and push for better if the right offer gives us room.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="fee-amount"><strong>~2.7%</strong></div>
      </div>
      <div class="fee-row fee-total">
        <div class="fee-label">
          <div class="fee-title">Total anticipated fees</div>
          <div class="fee-sub">Based on the recommended $565,000 list price.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="fee-amount"><strong>~5.2%</strong></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="net-proceeds">
      <div class="net-label">Estimated seller net at a $565,000 sale, closing 7/31/26</div>
      <div class="net-table">
        <div class="net-row">
          <div>Sale price</div>
          <div class="mono">$565,000.00</div>
        </div>
        <div class="net-row">
          <div>Settlement fee</div>
          <div class="mono">− $595.00</div>
        </div>
        <div class="net-row">
          <div>Conservation fee</div>
          <div class="mono">− $5.00</div>
        </div>
        <div class="net-row">
          <div>State deed tax</div>
          <div class="mono">− $1,864.50</div>
        </div>
        <div class="net-row">
          <div>My listing fee (2.5%)</div>
          <div class="mono">− $14,125.00</div>
        </div>
        <div class="net-row">
          <div>Buyer's agent compensation (2.7%)</div>
          <div class="mono">− $15,255.00</div>
        </div>
        <div class="net-row">
          <div>Transaction fee</div>
          <div class="mono">− $649.00</div>
        </div>
        <div class="net-row">
          <div>Prorated property taxes (credit from seller)</div>
          <div class="mono">− $469.64</div>
        </div>
        <div class="net-row net-final">
          <div>Estimated net proceeds to seller</div>
          <div class="mono"><strong>$532,036.86</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="net-note">
        Net sheet prepared by Trademark Title Services (Marti Mahoney-Peterson, Executive Closer) specifically for your home. This total doesn't yet include your mortgage payoff or your HELOC payoff. Once I have current payoff figures from both lenders, I'll get you an updated net sheet that reflects exactly what lands in your account at closing.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CLOSING -->
  <section class="closing">
    <div class="closing-inner">
      <div class="section-label-alt light">What's Next</div>
      <h2>When you're ready, I'm ready.</h2>
      <p>
        I know you're still working on some bigger questions, and I hope this piece of the puzzle helps. Whenever you decide, I can get everything in motion fast. Photography, staging, copy, MLS, marketing. If you're still targeting a late-ish summer close, we've got comfortable runway.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you want to talk through any of the numbers above, or just think out loud about the bigger picture, call or text me anytime.
      </p>

      <div class="closing-contact">
        <div class="closing-method">
          <span class="label">Call or Text</span>
          <a href="tel:+16122015447">612-201-5447</a>
        </div>
        <div class="closing-method">
          <span class="label">Email</span>
          <a href="mailto:mark@markgores.com">mark@markgores.com</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="closing-sign">Mark</p>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>

<footer class="prop-footer">
  <p>&copy; 2026 Mark Gores · RE/MAX Advantage Plus · Prior Lake, MN</p>
  <p class="footer-disclaimer">
    This pricing opinion is a good-faith estimate based on comparable sales data from NorthstarMLS as of April 2026. It is not an appraisal. Final sale price depends on market conditions at the time of listing, buyer demand, and property presentation. Information deemed reliable but not guaranteed.
  </p>
</footer>

</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Reuse global palette from BaseLayout */

  .proposal-nav {
    position: fixed;
    top: 0;
    width: 100%;
    padding: 1.25rem 3rem;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
    z-index: 100;
    background: rgba(245, 240, 232, 0.92);
    backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(10px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(139, 115, 85, 0.12);
  }
  .proposal-nav .name {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--dark);
    text-decoration: none;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .proposal-nav .nav-meta {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    color: var(--warm);
  }

  .proposal {
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  /* ===================== HERO ===================== */
  .prop-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr;
    gap: 4rem;
    align-items: center;
    min-height: 100vh;
    padding: 9rem 3rem 5rem;
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .prop-label {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    color: var(--warm);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .prop-label::before {
    content: '';
    display: block;
    width: 40px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--warm);
  }

  .prop-hero h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 5vw, 4.2rem);
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--dark);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
  .prop-hero h1 em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--accent);
    font-size: 0.7em;
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .prop-hero-text {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-light);
    max-width: 560px;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .prop-signature {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    color: var(--dark);
    font-style: italic;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .prop-hero-image {
    position: relative;
  }
  .prop-hero-image img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 4px;
    box-shadow: 0 20px 60px rgba(26, 26, 24, 0.15);
  }
  .photo-caption {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--warm);
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    text-align: right;
  }

  /* ===================== SECTION LABELS ===================== */
  .section-label-alt {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.65rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    color: var(--warm);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .section-label-alt::before {
    content: '';
    display: block;
    width: 24px;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--warm);
  }
  .section-label-alt.light { color: var(--accent); }
  .section-label-alt.light::before { background: var(--accent); }

  main.proposal section h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.5vw, 2.8rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--dark);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }
